# Worklog folder (memory for humans + new chats)

After meaningful implementation (and after user **go**), update `Worklog/` as below. **No secrets** (no keys, tokens, connection strings, `.env` values).

## Is this expensive? (follow these caps)

Worklogs **do use tokens** when written and when read. They save tokens if new chats `@` one short file instead of re-explaining the app.

**Hard caps (do not violate):**
- Do **not** paste full source code into Worklog files. Use **paths + line ranges** (e.g. `app/page.jsx` lines 40–85).
- Each feature file: prefer **≤40 lines**. Split only if a feature is huge.
- `Worklog/_ARCHITECTURE.md`: keep the map accurate; prefer **≤80 lines**.
- New Agent chat: read `@Worklog/_ARCHITECTURE.md` first. Read **one** feature file only if the task touches that feature. Do **not** load every file in `Worklog/` every turn.
- Skip Worklog updates for tiny one-line renames unless the user asks.
- Product **flow** prose (user/server/mock vs live) belongs in `Docs/how-it-works/` per `07-how-it-works.mdc`, not as a second Worklog tree.

## Folder layout

```text
Worklog/
  _ARCHITECTURE.md     ← overall map (update when folders/files appear)
  _CHANGELOG.md        ← newest entries at top (what happened this session)
  features/
    <feature-slug>.md  ← one file per feature/component slice
```

Create the folder on first implement if missing.

## `_ARCHITECTURE.md` (top of the “system” doc)

Keep this structure at the **top**, then a short stack note:

```markdown
# Architecture

## Folder map
| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| app/page.jsx | … |
| app/api/… | … |
| lib/… | … |
| components/… | … |
| Worklog/ | Human + agent memory (this folder) |

## Stack
Next.js App Router · Tailwind · shadcn · Supabase · Zod · Vercel

## Demo path
1. …
2. …
3. …

## Env (names only)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, …
```

Update the table when you add/remove important paths. Do not duplicate README.

## `_CHANGELOG.md` (everything that happened, brief)

Newest first. Each entry:

```markdown
### YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM — short title
- Did: …
- Files: `path` (lines a–b), `path2` (lines c–d)
- Feature doc: `Worklog/features/<slug>.md`
- Test: …
```

Max ~8 bullets per entry.

## `features/<slug>.md` (one per feature)

Slug examples: `home-ui`, `notes-api`, `supabase-wire`, `analyze-ai`.

```markdown
# <Feature name>

## Purpose
One paragraph.

## Files
| Path | Lines (approx) | What |
|------|----------------|------|
| app/api/notes/route.js | 1–80 | POST/GET notes |

## What we implemented
- Bullet list of behaviour (not code dumps)

## How to test
1. …
2. …

## Depends on
- env names / other features

## Out of scope
- …
```

## After each approved implementation

1. Update `Worklog/features/<slug>.md` (create or append).  
2. Prepend a short entry to `Worklog/_CHANGELOG.md`.  
3. Refresh `Worklog/_ARCHITECTURE.md` folder map if paths changed.  
4. In the chat **## Done** section, point Harry to the feature md path.

## Do not

- Replace the real codebase with docs (code is source of truth; Worklog is the map).
- Commit secrets into Worklog.
- Write novels or paste entire diffs.
- Create a new feature file for every tiny CSS tweak (append to the existing feature doc instead).
